# National TPA Scope — NON-NEGOTIABLE (ALL SECTORS)

**Dee Davis Inc. is a contract management TPA. DDI works nationwide — not Michigan-only. This applies to EVERY category, sector, service line, module, and outbound document.**

## The Rule

**Default company scope = United States (50 states + DC + territories where contracts require).**

DDI holds the client contract. DDI manages compliance, billing, QA, reporting, and escalation. DDI dispatches credentialed fulfillment partners **where the work is performed** — not where DDI is headquartered.

**Michigan (Troy HQ)** = headquarters, proof of operational discipline, and often **first mining priority** — **never** the geographic ceiling on capability statements, CO emails, proposals, rate sheets, bios, or strategy unless the solicitation explicitly limits place of performance.

## Applies To — ALL OF THESE

| Lane | Examples |
|------|----------|
| **Professional services** | Notary, CNTDA, RON, permit running, apostille, legal courier |
| **Testing & compliance** | DOT drug/alcohol TPA, DNA, lead, occ health, background screening |
| **Credentialing** | Fingerprinting (mobile/livescan), I-9, E-Verify program admin |
| **Transportation** | NEMT brokerage/TPA, medical courier, pharmacy delivery, freight, AOG |
| **Facilities** | Janitorial, landscaping, grounds, snow, facility maintenance |
| **Supply & product** | Industrial, medical supplies, equipment, reseller lanes |
| **Healthcare ops** | Lab courier, specimen transport, hospital support services |
| **Navigation / SDOH** | Benefits navigation, digital navigator, community partner programs |
| **Structured settlement / legal** | Settlement closings, vehicle title signings, estate signings |
| **Federal / state / local / MCO / commercial** | Every buyer type, every portal, every GPSS/DDCSS/PRISM/ATLAS bid |
| **HAVEN / disaster recovery** | Emergency TPA coordination — inherently multi-state |
| **Subsidiaries / DBAs** | 3D Ink, DePointe DNA, Freight 1st Direct, CNTDA — all under national TPA model |

**Cause We Care (501c3)** may have a **regional community service footprint** — that does NOT shrink **DDI's** contracting scope as prime/TPA.

## Required Default Language (Buyer-Facing)

- ✅ "Nationwide contract management TPA"
- ✅ "One contract with Dee Davis Inc. — fulfillment dispatched in all 50 states"
- ✅ "Headquartered in Troy, Michigan — national program administration"
- ✅ "In-person where required; RON / mobile / network dispatch per state rules"
- ✅ "EDWOSB prime — vendor diversity on national contracts"

## Banned Default Language (Company Scope)

- ❌ "Michigan only" / "Southeast Michigan only" / "Metro Detroit only" / "Michigan first" as **DDI service area**
- ❌ "We serve Michigan" without **also** stating national TPA dispatch
- ❌ "Local provider" as **DDI's identity** (local vendor preference in a **buyer's** RFP is fine to address)
- ❌ "Regional coverage" without national TPA framing
- ❌ Any draft that reads like a single-county shop instead of a **program-level TPA**

## When Local / State Geography IS OK

1. **Deliberate local hook** for a specific buyer (e.g., BBA Law "across the hall")
2. **Solicitation place of performance** is limited (bid to that — still note national TPA capacity for overflow/multi-site)
3. **Supplier/sub RFQs** — generic region only (never reveal buyer) — see buyer-protection rules
4. **Mining priority** — "check Michigan SIGMA first" = **where to hunt**, not **where DDI stops**
5. **Cause We Care** grant/community materials — actual nonprofit service area
6. **Pricing zones** — OK as **example dispatch pricing** if national TPA is stated first

## Sector-Specific Reminders

| Sector | National TPA framing |
|--------|---------------------|
| Drug testing | C/TPA — consortium, collectors, labs, MRO coordination nationwide |
| Fingerprinting | Capture + channel per contract; dispatch mobile/livescan nationally |
| NEMT | Program-level TPA above trip brokers; fulfillment partners under DDI contract |
| Courier / medical logistics | National network — never name consumer fulfillment brands to prospects |
| Janitorial / grounds | Prime manages subs in **each** contract geography |
| Federal CO outreach | SAM-registered, nationwide capability — micro-purchase/SAT thresholds |
| MCO / Medicaid | Enroll per state; **model** scales state-by-state — not Michigan-only MCO shop |

## Hard Stop

Before presenting **any** buyer-facing document, email, cap statement, proposal, rate sheet, or strategy summary:

- [ ] Does this read as **national TPA** or **local vendor**?
- [ ] If local geography appears, is it a **hook** or an **accidental scope limit**?
- [ ] Are all **service lines** in the doc consistent (not notary=national but fingerprinting=Michigan-only)?

**If it reads like a local shop — rewrite before showing Dee.**

